CorvCAD patch series for KiCad 10.0.6 (caf7377): keep the schematic model free of editor code.

Applied by integrations/kicad_core/fetch.py. Each change keeps the desktop editor working
(the full probe still links and matches kicad-cli); split per item before sending upstream.

1. Schematic items: check the frame type with IsType( FRAME_SCH ) and read the current sheet
   from the item's own SCHEMATIC instead of casting to SCH_EDIT_FRAME (bus entry, junction,
   line, label, pin, symbol, sheet message panels).
2. SCHEMATIC_HOLDER gains HeldSchematic(), AddItemToSelection(), RemoveItemFromSelection()
   and RecalculateConnectivity(); SCHEMATIC::CleanUp(), EESCHEMA_HELPERS::LoadSchematic()
   and ERC_TESTER::RunTests() use them instead of SCH_SELECTION_TOOL / SCH_EDIT_FRAME.
3. LoadSchematic() no longer creates (and leaks) a frame-less TOOL_MANAGER; SCH_COMMIT
   accepts a null tool manager.
4. Hypertext: items call the virtual SCH_BASE_FRAME::HypertextCommand(), and
   SCH_NAVIGATE_TOOL::g_BackLink is an inline header constant.
5. Editor-only code moves next to its editors: ERC_TREE_MODEL::GetValue() to dialog_erc.cpp,
   SCH_FIELD::OnScintillaCharAdded() to dialog_field_properties.cpp,
   SCH_TEXT::ShowSyntaxHelp() to dialog_text_properties.cpp, STATUSBAR_WARNING_REPORTER to
   widgets/kistatusbar.cpp. SCH_PLOTTER loses its SCH_EDIT_FRAME constructor.
6. Field validation rules move to common/field_validation.cpp (no wx validator), used by
   FIELD_VALIDATOR and SCH_SYMBOL::SetRefProp() (which now logs instead of a message box).
7. LEGACY_SYMBOL_LIBS::LoadAllLibraries() takes an optional PROGRESS_REPORTER instead of
   opening APP_PROGRESS_DIALOG; PROJECT_SCH::LegacySchLibs() reports load errors via wxLog.
8. SCH_IO_DATABASE creates its settings dialog through a factory the eeschema module sets.
